Scoring (0–100 composite)
Weights are tunable; start:

Intent score (0–25): question words, “for {industry}”, “for small business”, “near me”, “services”, “consultant”. Bonus for {industry} + {task} combos.

Opportunity score (0–35): volume (log-scaled), growth (Trends slope), competition (lower is better), CPC (proxy for commercial value). 
DataForSEO

Difficulty score (0–20, inverted): 100 − KD. Clamp if KD > 70. 
DataForSEO

SERP win factors (0–20): if SERP shows featured snippet/People Also Ask/local pack/AI overview with weak content, boost. (Derived from Live SERP inspection.) 
DataForSEO

Selection

Cut by KD & min volume (e.g., KD ≤ 55; SV ≥ 20 if high intent; SV ≥ 10 if geo).

Take top N overall and also ensure coverage buckets: each industry gets ≥X winners; each high-value task ≥Y.

4) Page strategy per keyword (what the generator must produce)

Each landing page must:

Mirror the exact query in <title>, <h1>, and intro (“answer first”).

Provide an actionable solution: 3–7 steps, a mini-tool/checklist/template, plus industry-specific examples.

Include a soft CTA (“If you’d like help implementing this, here’s how we work with {industry} teams.”).

Internal links to 2–3 relevant hub pages & 2 cross-industry case studies.

Geo variation (if geo term present): local proof points, regulations, examples, and a different CTA snippet (hours, service area, contact).

Unique value: At least two concrete, industry-specific examples and one downloadable/interactive element to avoid doorway/thin content risks. 
